      <title>Airport operator loses claim against Greece over rental fees</title>
      <link>https://globalarbitrationreview.com/article/airport-operator-loses-claim-against-greece-over-rental-fees</link>
      <description>An LCIA tribunal has sided with Greece in a €30 million rent dispute with the operator of the country’s busiest airport, while rejecting the state’s argument that it lacked jurisdiction over the contractual case because of the ECJ decision in Achmea.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://globalarbitrationreview.com/article/airport-operator-loses-claim-against-greece-over-rental-fees</guid>
